{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793656527,"nonce":"y74dLaEDjIzLaFQPeunitDF3QPw=","title":"Push Cloud Sync document updates with bounded reconnect and durable acknowledgements","message":"Parent: cd54ac37bbbdfea0fa1fcd39288738a7c0b48475ed9ecea3e6cc98ad20c109ed. Prerequisite: 644a5dd shared history/exchange foundation. Coordinate with the editor-binding issue.\n\nAdd authenticated subscription delivery over a workspace-scoped transport, reusing the canonical journal rather than a second edit history. Use Durable Object hibernation or another event-driven wait; no idle HTTP polling. Bind subscriptions and every message to account/workspace/path/lineage, enforce existing expiry and write permissions, and keep publish/control credentials out of browser messages.\n\nBound connection/document counts, message and queued bytes, retries and backpressure. Acknowledgements follow the atomic journal commit; notifications do not imply durability on their own. On reconnect exchange the accepted frontier and journal sequence, including deletion-only history even when vectors are unchanged. Deduplicate retried deltas, reject missing dependencies, pause retired/rebound lineages and release watchers/graphs when the last consumer closes. Token expiry and revocation must fence existing connections as well as new ones.\n\nTest concurrent clients, slow/offline peers, lost replies, queue overflow, storage refusal, snapshot publication and recreation, gateway/session/VM replacement, cleanup and idle wakeups. A real deployed Cloudflare test is still needed to validate hibernation/edge/runtime behavior after local fixtures pass.","files":null}]}